Some of the tracks on this board cross.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.4,2.6);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.6);
\coordinate (E) at (1.7,3.8);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (C)--(D);
\draw (D)--(A);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (D)--(E);
\draw (E)--(B);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Is this graph planar?

